design_tokens:
**Color Tokens (all defined on `:root`, dark-first, no light mode).**
```css
:root {
  /* Surfaces */
  --bg:              #05070A;
  --bg-elevated:     #0B0F14;
  --bg-sunken:       #030507;
  --surface:         #0F141B;
  --surface-hover:   #141B24;
  --border:          rgba(0, 255, 156, 0.08);
  --border-strong:   rgba(0, 255, 156, 0.16);
  --border-focus:    rgba(0, 255, 156, 0.48);

  /* Text */
  --fg:              #E6F7EE;    /* primary, ~15:1 on --bg */
  --fg-muted:        #8A9BA2;    /* labels, meta */
  --fg-subtle:       #4A5B62;    /* disabled, timestamps */
  --fg-inverse:      #05070A;    /* on --accent solid */

  /* Signal colors */
  --accent:          #00FF9C;    /* matrix green, primary */
  --accent-hover:    #33FFB4;
  --accent-press:    #00CC7D;
  --accent-wash:     rgba(0, 255, 156, 0.12);
  --matrix-glow:     rgba(0, 255, 156, 0.35);
  --matrix-rain:     #00FF41;    /* reserved for code rain + rabbit eye-trail */

  --danger:          #FFB020;    /* amber warn/destructive */
  --danger-wash:     rgba(255, 176, 32, 0.14);
  --info:            #22D3EE;    /* cyan */
  --info-wash:       rgba(34, 211, 238, 0.12);
  --success:         #00FF9C;    /* alias of --accent */
  --error:           #FF4D6D;    /* only for validation/broken state, not "danger" */

  /* Tier colors — badge borders, rank chips, node ring on map */
  --tier-apprentice:   #8A9BA2;  /* cool gray */
  --tier-practitioner: #22D3EE;  /* cyan */
  --tier-expert:       #FFB020;  /* amber */
  --tier-elite:        #FF3EA5;  /* magenta, sparingly */
}
```

**Radii.** `--radius-xs: 4px` (chips, inline code), `--radius-sm: 6px` (buttons, inputs), `--radius-md: 10px` (cards, tiles), `--radius-lg: 14px` (sheets, dialogs), `--radius-xl: 20px` (hero surfaces), `--radius-pill: 999px`. The map node itself is a hexagon rendered as SVG polygon, not a border-radius.

**Spacing scale.** 4-based, no half-steps: `--space-0: 0`, `--space-1: 4px`, `--space-2: 8px`, `--space-3: 12px`, `--space-4: 16px`, `--space-5: 24px`, `--space-6: 32px`, `--space-7: 48px`, `--space-8: 64px`, `--space-9: 96px`, `--space-10: 128px`. Layout gutters on the hub are `--space-6`; card padding is `--space-5`; button padding is `--space-3 --space-4`.

**Type scale (Geist Mono display / Inter body).**
`--fs-xs: 11px` (map node labels, hotkey chips) · `--fs-sm: 13px` (secondary UI, badges) · `--fs-base: 15px` (body) · `--fs-md: 17px` (subheadings) · `--fs-lg: 20px` (card titles) · `--fs-xl: 28px` (page titles) · `--fs-2xl: 40px` (hero) · `--fs-3xl: 64px` (landing hero, tabular XP counter on level-up). Line heights: `--lh-tight: 1.15` (display), `--lh-snug: 1.35` (UI), `--lh-normal: 1.55` (body). Tracking: `--tracking-tight: -0.02em` (display Geist Mono), `--tracking-body: -0.005em` (Inter), `--tracking-wide: 0.06em` (all-caps labels, kept small `--fs-xs`).

**Shadows / Glow.**
```css
--shadow-1: 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.02) inset,
            0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.4);
--shadow-2: 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.03) inset,
            0 8px 24px -8px rgba(0,0,0,0.6);
--shadow-glow-accent: 0 0 0 1px var(--border-focus),
                     0 0 24px rgba(0,255,156,0.25),
                     0 0 60px rgba(0,255,156,0.10);
--shadow-glow-elite:  0 0 0 1px rgba(255,62,165,0.5),
                     0 0 32px rgba(255,62,165,0.28);
--shadow-node-active: 0 0 0 2px var(--accent),
                     0 0 28px var(--matrix-glow);
--shadow-tile-hover: 0 12px 32px -12px rgba(0,255,156,0.25),
                    0 0 0 1px var(--border-strong);
```

**Motion tokens.** `--ease-spring: cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.72, 0, 1)` (fallback for CSS), `--ease-out: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)`, `--dur-fast: 120ms`, `--dur-base: 220ms`, `--dur-slow: 400ms`, `--dur-hero: 800ms`. Framer Motion uses spring configs directly (see visual_theme).

**Z-index scale.** `--z-rain: 0`, `--z-content: 10`, `--z-nav: 30`, `--z-sheet: 40`, `--z-dialog: 50`, `--z-popover: 60`, `--z-toast: 70`, `--z-cursor: 80` (magnetic cursor).

level_map_design:
**Rendering stack.** The map is a single `<svg>` element (viewBox coordinates in "world units" where 1 unit = 100px at zoom 1.0) with three logical layers, top to bottom: (1) an HTML `<div>` behind the SVG for the code-rain canvas and parallax mist; (2) the SVG itself, split into `<g>` layers — `edges`, `nodes`, `labels`, `rabbit`, `carrot`; (3) an HTML overlay for HUD elements (mini-map, zoom controls, breadcrumb of current track). Framer Motion drives node/edge transforms via `motion.g` and `motion.path`; the SVG root's transform is animated by a single `useSpring`-driven `transform: translate(camX, camY) scale(zoom)` so the whole world moves as one, avoiding per-node layout thrash.

**Node/edge data model.** Consumed as JSON from the MAP_SCHEMA agent's output. Every node is:
```ts
type Node = {
  id: string;                    // "sqli-01"
  slug: string;                  // route slug for /lab/[cat]/[slug]
  track: TrackId;                // "sql" | "xss" | "ssrf" | ...
  tier: "apprentice"|"practitioner"|"expert"|"elite";
  title: string;
  x: number; y: number;          // world coords, y grows upward
  status: "locked"|"available"|"in_progress"|"solved"|"boss";
  requires: string[];            // ids that must be solved to unlock
  xp: number;
  isBoss?: boolean;              // renders larger hex with amber ring
  isDaily?: boolean;             // pulses cyan
};
type Edge = {
  from: string; to: string;
  kind: "linear"|"branch"|"gate";
  powered: boolean;              // true when `from` is solved
};
```
Nodes render as **flat-top hexagons**, 48px radius at zoom 1.0, 32px stroke-width for the ring in tier color. Boss nodes are 72px radius with an amber double-ring and a small skull glyph. Locked nodes desaturate to `--fg-subtle` with a padlock glyph centered; available nodes pulse a 2-second `opacity` breath on the outer ring (disabled under reduced-motion). Solved nodes fill with `--accent-wash` and show a check glyph; a subtle inner glow `--matrix-glow` at 40% opacity marks them.

**Edges.** Bézier paths (`<path>`) between nodes, ~2px stroke. When `powered: false`, stroke is `--border` (dim) and dash `4 6`; when `powered: true`, stroke animates to `--accent`, dash offset animates infinitely (`stroke-dashoffset` from 0 → −20 over 1.6s linear) creating a "current flowing" effect. Branch/gate edges thicken to 3px and get a subtle amber outer glow at gate junctions.

**Camera follows rabbit.** The rabbit's position `(rx, ry)` is a spring-driven `useSpring`. A `useEffect` watches the target node id (the "next objective") and animates the camera such that the rabbit sits at 40% from the bottom of the viewport (i.e. camera target = `-rx + vw/2`, `-ry + vh*0.6`). User pan/zoom (wheel + drag with pointer capture) *temporarily* releases camera-follow for 4 seconds after last input, then re-engages. A small "recenter on rabbit" HUD button forces re-engage immediately.

**Zoom levels.** Three semantic zooms with snap-affinity: **Overview** (0.35x, all tracks visible, labels hidden below `--fs-xs`, edges thinned), **Track** (1.0x, default, node labels visible), **Node** (1.8x, node stats overlay appears — XP reward, avg solve time, first-blood holder). Zoom is animated with the standard soft spring and clamped `[0.25, 2.4]`. Ctrl/Cmd + scroll or pinch on trackpad; `+/−` keys as fallback; `0` resets to Track zoom on rabbit.

**Performance for 400+ nodes.** Virtualize by culling: on every `requestAnimationFrame`, compute the visible world-rect and set `display: none` on `<g>` node groups outside a 1.2x-expanded viewport. Edges are cheap enough to leave in but stroke-render only if either endpoint is visible. Node visuals are memoized React components keyed by id and status — a status change rerenders one node, not the tree. Text labels use `<text>` with `pointer-events: none`; hover/click uses an invisible enlarged `<circle>` for a bigger hit target. The code-rain canvas caps at 60fps via `requestAnimationFrame`, reduces to 30fps when the tab is not focused, and pauses when the map is being actively panned (detected via a `isPanning` ref) to keep drag latency <16ms.

**"Powered-up" edges on solve.** When a solve toast fires, the edge(s) leaving that node run a one-shot animation: (a) stroke color transitions `--border` → `--accent` over 300ms, (b) a "pulse" of brighter green (`#33FFB4`) travels from source to target via a `<circle>` moving along the path using `getPointAtLength` at 60fps for 900ms, (c) after the pulse arrives, the target node transitions from `locked` → `available` with a 400ms scale-spring from 0.85 → 1.0 and its ring lights up. Batched — if multiple edges unlock, they stagger by 80ms.
